// ============================================================================
// Detection: Cryptocurrency Mining in Container
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1496 - Resource Hijacking
// Source: ContainerLogV2 + InsightsMetrics
// ============================================================================

// HOW THIS DETECTION WORKS
// -------------------------
// Crypto mining (T1496 Resource Hijacking) steals the cluster's CPU to mine coins.
// There are two complementary ways to catch it, and this file ships both:
//
//   1. PROCESS/SIGNATURE (active below): scan container logs for the fingerprints
//      of miners — binary names (xmrig, minerd), mining-pool protocol strings
//      (stratum+tcp), algorithm names (cryptonight), and known pool hostnames.
//   2. CPU ANOMALY (commented out): watch resource metrics for sustained high CPU,
//      which catches unknown/renamed miners that leave no signature.
//
// The signature approach is precise (low false positives) but misses novel miners;
// the anomaly approach is the safety net. In production you'd run both.

// --- Approach 1: signature match on container stdout/stderr -------------------
// TABLE: ContainerLogV2 — collected container console output.
ContainerLogV2
| where TimeGenerated > ago(1h)          // recent window first
// has_any = match if the log line contains ANY of these tokens. Mix of binary
// names, pool-protocol markers, and a known pool hostname — the miner's fingerprints.
| where LogMessage has_any ("xmrig", "minerd", "stratum+tcp", "cryptonight", "pool.minexmr")
| project TimeGenerated, PodName, PodNamespace, ContainerName, LogMessage  // analyst-relevant columns
| extend MitreTechnique = "T1496"        // tag with the ATT&CK technique

// --- Approach 2: CPU anomaly (DISABLED — reference implementation) ------------
// Enable when signature coverage isn't enough; catches renamed/unknown miners.
// TABLE: InsightsMetrics — the Azure Monitor container metrics table.
// InsightsMetrics
// | where TimeGenerated > ago(1h)
// | where Namespace == "container.azm.ms/cpu"        // the CPU metric namespace
// | where Name == "cpuUsageNanoCores"                // per-container CPU usage counter
// | extend Tags = parse_json(Tags)                   // Tags is JSON; parse to read podName/podNamespace
// | where todouble(Val) > 1800000000 // >1.8 cores sustained = suspicious
// | project TimeGenerated, PodName = tostring(Tags.podName), Namespace = tostring(Tags.podNamespace), CpuNanoCores = Val
